> import: decisions:
  BooleanCriteria
  ChoiceCriteria
  Probability
  Rubric

```
from kedi import Constraints
```

~Delivery(
  damaged: Annotated[
    bool,
    `BooleanCriteria(true="The evidence explicitly says the delivery arrived damaged.", false="The delivery was undamaged or its condition is unknown.")`
  ],
  damage_probability: Annotated[
    Probability,
    `BooleanCriteria(true="The evidence explicitly says the delivery arrived damaged.", false="The delivery was undamaged or its condition is unknown.")`
  ]
)

~Assessment(
  delivery: Delivery,
  category: Annotated[
    Literal["billing", "technical"],
    `ChoiceCriteria({"billing": "The customer reports an incorrect charge or invoice.", "technical": "The customer reports a software crash or malfunction."})`
  ],
  quality: Annotated[
    float,
    "Score only the proposed arithmetic answer against the reference.",
    `Constraints(ge=0, le=2)`,
    `Rubric(["Contradicts the reference", "Partially correct", "Matches the reference"])`
  ]
)

>> Given <evidence>, the assessment is [review: Assessment].
= ```
return {
    "damaged": review.delivery.damaged,
    "probability_positive": review.delivery.damage_probability > 0.85,
    "category": review.category,
    "accepted": review.quality >= 1.5,
}
```
